      <li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/newfound-galaxy-class-may-indicate-early-black-hole-growth-webb-finds/">NASA Webb Mission Team (2025), <em>Newfound Galaxy Class May Indicate Early Black Hole Growth</em></a> &mdash; the large early census, its redshift distribution and initial broad-line evidence.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09900-4">Rusakov et al. (2026), <em>Little red dots as young supermassive black holes in dense ionized cocoons</em>, Nature</a> &mdash; electron-scattering line profiles and reduced black-hole masses.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10579-4">Juodžbalis et al. (2026), <em>A direct black-hole mass measurement in a little red dot at high redshift</em>, Nature</a> &mdash; the resolved rotation curve of Abell2744-QSO1.</li>
      <li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasa-webb-finds-strongest-evidence-yet-for-black-hole-stars/">NASA/ESA/CSA Webb (2026), <em>Webb Finds Strongest Evidence Yet for Black Hole Stars</em></a> &mdash; GLIMPSE-17775 and its line-rich lensed spectrum.</li>
