      <li><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41550-026-02945-z">Zhang et al. (2026), <em>Extended components of little red dots in the rest-frame optical</em>, Nature Astronomy</a> &mdash; stacked evidence for compact stellar hosts.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10985-8">Chon et al. (2026), <em>Overmassive black holes and little red dots naturally form in simulations</em>, Nature</a> &mdash; a heavy-seed and rapid-growth pathway.</li>
      <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/ae4596">Ma et al. (2026), <em>Counting Little Red Dots at \(z&lt;4\)</em>, The Astrophysical Journal</a> &mdash; the declining lower-redshift abundance and its selection caveats.</li>
