<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="lede">Webb did not break cosmology by finding red points. It found a population that forced
      astronomers to stop assigning every photon to the first familiar source. The dots became intelligible
      when the light was allowed to have a journey: made near a black hole, transformed by gas, mixed with a
      young host, stretched by the universe, and finally separated again by a telescope.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Return to <a href="/essays/">the essays</a>, or compare the framework&rsquo;s explicit
      physical tests in <a href="/stress-tests/">the stress tests</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
